WEBVTT

00:00:00.001 --> 00:00:35.714
Three Proxmox nodes in a cluster, and a client on the same network. One of the containers will survive the death of its node.

00:00:35.814 --> 00:00:47.066
One command installs it all: three automated Proxmox installs, the client, then the cluster. About forty minutes, so here it is already running.

00:00:47.166 --> 00:01:10.242
The cluster: three nodes, quorate. Corosync runs on the lab segment, and the quorum is the majority: two nodes out of three are enough.

00:01:10.342 --> 00:01:26.991
Node one runs two LXC containers. The first, IT-Tools, has its disk on ZFS and an address on the lab network.

00:01:27.091 --> 00:01:58.026
Its disk lives on node one only. Two replication jobs send it to the other nodes with ZFS, then every minute only the changes.

00:01:58.126 --> 00:02:12.375
Now high availability: the cluster takes care of the container, and restarts it elsewhere if its node disappears.

00:02:12.475 --> 00:02:40.029
The web interface of node two shows the same: the container under node one, managed by HA.

00:02:40.129 --> 00:03:01.665
On the client, a loop asks for the page every five seconds.

00:03:01.765 --> 00:03:12.465
And now we pull the plug on node one: hold the power button for two seconds, and QEMU stops at once. No shutdown.

00:03:12.565 --> 00:03:21.033
The other two keep the quorum. After a minute, HA marks the dead node to be fenced, and waits for its lock to expire.

00:03:21.133 --> 00:03:35.538
Two and a half minutes later the container runs on node two, from the last replica.

00:03:35.638 --> 00:03:47.019
And the client? A few minutes without an answer, then the same page, at the same address.

00:03:47.119 --> 00:04:37.496
Node one comes back and rejoins. The replication now runs the other way, and one command brings the container home.

00:04:37.596 --> 00:05:30.164
Five tests, one per exercise. The last one pulls the plug again, by itself.

00:05:30.264 --> 00:05:39.456 line:6%
Every command is in the guide, in English and Italian, from the lab's card.
